      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1">The framed manuscript page number [ⲕⲅ] is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke. In ⲛϥⲩⲡⲁⲣⲭⲟⲩ the measured stroke (909–927) is centred over the junction of ⲛ and ϥ and covers each by 53 %, so it is encoded on both; so also ⲛϥ in l. 2 (57 %, 58 %) and l. 5 (57 %, 58 %).</p>
        <p n="2">Two separate strokes: one over ⲛϥ and one over the first ⲙ of ⲛϥⲙⲙⲉ (measured 526–544 and 555–568); all four letters ⲛϥⲙⲙ carry a sublinear dot.</p>
        <p n="8">The line ends with an opening bracket and nothing after it (lost to the end of the line); so also l. 9.</p>
        <p n="10">An enlarged ⲧ stands after ⲛⲉⲩ; the ten dots after it are printed more closely spaced than elsewhere.</p>
        <p n="11">An enlarged ⲛ begins ⲛⲉ[ⲓ]ⲉⲧϥ after the closing bracket.</p>
        <p n="14">Chapter opening: the numeral ⲅ (3) centred with an overline; the title follows in ll. 15–16.</p>
        <p n="15">The marginal numerals ([ⲅ] left, ⲅ right, both with overline) stand between the two title lines (y ≈ 952); they are attached to l. 15.</p>
        <p n="17">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲡ inside the restoration. The edition opens a bracket before ⲡ at the line end and does not close it; it is closed here.</p>
        <p n="18">Measured stroke over ϩⲛ (699–718): ϩ 50 %, ⲛ 57 %, encoded on both. The stroke over the final ⲥ of ⲧⲥⲁⲩϩⲥ is printed obliquely.</p>
        <p n="20">The second ϣ of ϣⲟⲩϣ[ⲟ]ⲩ has a sublinear dot in its lower bowl (8× zoom; the first ϣ, undotted, has none); so also ϣ in ll. 22 and 24.</p>
        <p n="22">Measured stroke over ϩⲙ (862–886): ϩ 56 %, ⲙ 70 %, encoded on both.</p>
        <p n="32">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲧ inside the restoration.</p>
        <p n="33">The restored [ⲡⲟⲩⲁⲓⲛⲉ] is printed with sublinear dots under ⲟⲩⲁⲓⲛ inside the brackets.</p>
      </div>
